    "body": "## Summary\n\nGiteeService.getUpdate assigns Constant.GITEE_TOKEN, which the supplied source defines as a compile-time string literal, as the Kotlin default for its parameter annotated @Query(\"access_token\"). This establishes the reported hard-coded access-token source flow.\n\nRemove the compile-time literal from the default value of the Retrofit access_token query parameter. Use a maintainer-approved authentication or credential-provisioning path rather than embedding a reusable value in the client API default, while preserving the applicable callable and endpoint-authentication contracts.\n\nChanges:\n\n- `network-api/src/main/java/com/hfut/schedule/network/api/inf/GiteeService.kt`: Removes Constant.GITEE_TOKEN from the default access_token query-value flow while preserving getUpdate's name, no-argument callability, explicit credential binding, and existing page defaults.\n- `app/src/androidTest/java/com/hfut/schedule/GiteeServiceRequestContractTest.kt`: Adds Android instrumentation coverage for local Retrofit request construction only. The test verifies that the no-argument entry point omits access_token and that an explicitly supplied non-reusable runtime credential is bound as access_token without executing a request.\n\n## How was this tested?\n\n- [x] Automated test coverage added in 1 test file(s)\n- [x] Project compiles successfully (`:app:assembleDebugAndroidTest`)\n\n## Additional context\n\nI’m an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\n\nI’m happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project’s architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers’ recommendations.",
